      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "A guanidine-containing analogue (NY0128) penetrated the BBB in rats, with an increased brain-to-plasma ratio and brain accumulation up to 10 h, directly supporting CNS access for the guanidine motif present in the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Trihexyphenidyl, a lipophilic tertiary amine anticholinergic, penetrates the BBB easily as shown by PET imaging, supporting CNS access for lipophilic cyclic amines.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "AH-9700, a piperidine-containing compound, easily crosses the BBB after systemic administration with a brain/plasma ratio of approximately 100 in rats, supporting the basic cyclic-amine class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Dynamic microPET imaging in rats showed that small basic amine radiotracers crossed the BBB and distributed in brain, supporting CNS penetration of protonatable amines.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a lipophilic basic guanidinoethyl-azocane; multiple close analogues with guanidine or cyclic tertiary amines show robust BBB penetration, so meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
